Package: perch
Version: 1.2.1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-psutil, python3-yaml
Recommends: python3-gi, gir1.2-webkit2-4.0, python3-openpyxl, python3-docx
Suggests: google-chrome-stable, docker.io
Maintainer: Perch contributors <perch@example.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/dwarka-prasad/perch
Description: Perch — local system and developer dashboard
 Perch is a single-binary web dashboard for managing your Linux machine:
 live CPU/memory/GPU/disk/network charts, process and service control,
 storage analysis and cleanup, a whole-system file search, log viewer,
 kernel tunables, package management, laptop settings (brightness, volume,
 Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, wallpaper, theme), a developer toolbox (HTTP tester,
 JSON/YAML, regex, diff, converters), and an AI assistant backed by the
 local Claude CLI. It binds to 127.0.0.1 and is protected by an access token.
